<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:42:03 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>MAGA: Why Trump's movement is fracturing?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-maga-why-trump-s-movement-is-fracturing</link><description>
As the 2026 midterm elections approach, divisions within the MAGA camp are becoming increasingly visible. From the war in Iran and rising fuel prices to the Epstein files, several of Trump’s decisions are fuelling divisions among his most loyal supporters.
 
Once united by a shared vision of America, MAGA now brings together factions that increasingly disagree over foreign policy, the economy and what “America First” should actually mean. Yet Trump remains the central figure holding this political coalition together – and he is fighting to keep it that way.
 
Why are some of the president’s longtime allies distancing themselves from him? Can MAGA remain united despite these disagreements? And can Trump still mobilise his base ahead of the midterms?
 
🔍 Our journalist Stella Elgersma breaks down the divisions within the MAGA movement and Donald Trump’s strategy to rally his supporters, once again.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/baf97aaa-d481-11f1-9162-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-maga-definiti.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/baf97aaa-d481-11f1-9162-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/minia-maga-definiti.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06cd1536-d3c4-11f1-a268-b78df76b8b0e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:01:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Deeply hurt': Convicted murderer Christa Pike speaks out after botched execution</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-deeply-hurt-convicted-murderer-christa-pike-speaks-out-after-botched-execution</link><description>
Tennessee death row inmate Christa Pike said she remains in constant pain after surviving a botched lethal injection in September, in her first public statement since the failed execution. She expressed gratitude for those who saved her life while urging compassion for her victim's family.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04ffd4cc-bcfa-11f1-b6d4-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T050004Z-1357594743-RC2GTNA3DKIY-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04ffd4cc-bcfa-11f1-b6d4-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T050004Z-1357594743-RC2GTNA3DKIY-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf52098a-d473-11f1-a717-79497bb54489</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:29:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/04ffd4cc-bcfa-11f1-b6d4-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T050004Z-1357594743-RC2GTNA3DKIY-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg">© Tenessee Department of Correction, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>How will the women's vote shape the US midterms?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261030-how-will-the-women-s-vote-shape-the-us-midterms</link><description>
With the US midterms approaching, we examine the power of the women's vote in an election that will shape the balance of power in Washington during Donald Trump’s final two years in office. Annette Young talks to Annie Karni, congressional correspondent for The New York Times and Kelly Dittmar, Director of Research at the Centre for American Women and Politics.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e8dc1a2-d465-11f1-bafa-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/web-photo-51-percent-midterms.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e8dc1a2-d465-11f1-bafa-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/web-photo-51-percent-midterms.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed2bea6e-d466-11f1-bc3d-417feb7fc806</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:52:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Texas Republicans accused of changing electoral rules ahead of midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261030-texas-republicans-accused-of-changing-electoral-rules-ahead-of-midterms</link><description>
With the US midterm elections approaching, Republicans in Texas are being accused of changing electoral rules in their favour. In Tarrant County, near Dallas, they've cut the number of election-day polling places by nearly 30 percent. The decision is being challenged in court and adds to last year's state-wide redistricting, a move designed to benefit Republicans. But the measures could also help galvanise the Democratic opposition. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent reports, with Wassim Cornet.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cba8206-d3be-11f1-a12f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-USA-TEXAS-GERRYMANDERING-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cba8206-d3be-11f1-a12f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-USA-TEXAS-GERRYMANDERING-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d5933fc-d3be-11f1-85c4-6facf1c0b072</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:07:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Pierrick LEURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>‘Scared of crossing the border’: The Arizona farmers who rely on Mexican workers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261030-scared-of-crossing-the-border-the-arizona-farmers-who-rely-on-mexican-workers</link><description>
The vast produce farms of Yuma County, Arizona, rely heavily on foreign workers who cross the border every day from Mexico. John Boelts, a farmer and staunch supporter of US President Donald Trump, praises the administration’s strict border controls – though he says that competing Republican factions have complicated efforts to hire foreign labourers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f106d570-d44f-11f1-a61e-a30f742156bf</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:28:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e2330d6-cbd4-11f1-a9eb-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/main-dans-les-champs.jpg">© Barbara Gabel, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Barbara GABEL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: With deep-red states now in play, could blue wave redraw America's political landscape?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-with-deep-red-states-now-in-play-could-blue-wave-redraw-america-s-political-landscape</link><description><![CDATA[
With the US approaching a potentially consequential midterm election, the political landscape appears to be shifting. Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Dr Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics & Policy at Queen Mary University of London, who examines the prospect of a sweeping Democratic victory. He argues that the party could achieve gains of a magnitude not seen since Barack Obama's historic presidential election in 2008. Johnson sees a combination of Democratic enthusiasm, and growing support among independents, white college-educated voters and Latinos, and signs of defections from Donald Trump's fiercely loyal electoral coalition.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b809dbc-d440-11f1-99fe-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-081145-082119-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b809dbc-d440-11f1-99fe-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261030-081145-082119-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90f2d4fe-d440-11f1-b12e-5b70a4bef21c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:30:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Michigan's El-Sayed targeted by Republicans in midterms race: Will the religion card work?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261029-michigan-s-el-sayed-targeted-by-republicans-in-midterms-race-will-the-religion-card-work</link><description>
What in the name of political free speech is off limits? Can you say whatever you want on the campaign trail, no matter how false or racist it is? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/630dd734-d452-11f1-871f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7cff6987.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/630dd734-d452-11f1-871f-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7cff6987.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4cd9460c-d3cf-11f1-bdb3-d5b6d9e86fc7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:31:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Lt. Gen. Ben Hodges accuses Hegseth of 'getting rid of people who may have the courage to push back'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/lt-gen-ben-hodges-accuses-hegseth-of-getting-rid-of-people-who-may-have-the-courage-to-push-back</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Lt. General (ret.) Ben Hodges, former commander of US Army Europe and NATO Allied Land Command. The dismissal of senior military officers without public explanation raises fundamental questions about institutional trust and the relationship between civilian authority and military leadership. For General Hodges, the reported firing of Lt. General Brett Sylvia reflects a potentially troubling pattern within the Pentagon under Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Equally striking is his criticism of the reluctance of retired senior commanders to speak publicly against policies they consider damaging. Hodges said he was "disappointed and surprised" by the limited public resistance among former four-star generals.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ee055ada-d3bf-11f1-980e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261029-161020-161914-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ee055ada-d3bf-11f1-980e-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261029-161020-161914-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f395a464-d3bf-11f1-8428-7d5b7c2908c6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:09:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro’s great escape: Is this the beginning of the end for ‘Bolsonarism’?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261029-flavio-bolsonaro-s-great-escape-is-this-the-beginning-of-the-end-for-bolsonarism</link><description>
The Brazilian election results had barely been announced before the defeated presidential candidate, Flavio Bolsonaro, packed his bags and fled with his family to the United States. The move may have dealt a serious blow to the already tarnished family brand, but does it spell the end for “Bolsonarism”?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bce0bc2-d313-11f1-a9f3-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-28T162830Z-1795241932-RC2ECOA4ORF6-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-USA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bce0bc2-d313-11f1-a9f3-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-28T162830Z-1795241932-RC2ECOA4ORF6-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-USA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48d1927a-d3a3-11f1-83bb-417e104b62ef</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:19:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bce0bc2-d313-11f1-a9f3-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-28T162830Z-1795241932-RC2ECOA4ORF6-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-USA.jpg">© Eva Marie Uzcategui, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ireland opens arms to Americans fleeing US President Donald Trump</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-ireland-opens-arms-to-americans-fleeing-us-president-donald-trump</link><description>
Tens of thousands of US citizens have fled the United States since Donald Trump's return to power two years ago. Given the language and a shared history, Ireland has been among the top choices for Americans looking for an alternative. FRANCE 24's team reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f220fdc-d3a7-11f1-940f-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-50d6a632.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f220fdc-d3a7-11f1-940f-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-50d6a632.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">080c43f0-d3a5-11f1-85cb-893570fa81c2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:31:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Midterms: Donald Trump and Barack Obama make closing pitches</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-us-midterms-donald-trump-and-barack-obama-make-closing-pitches</link><description>
In the United States, Democrats are turning to Barack Obama to rally voters ahead of the midterm elections, a crucial test that could shape the remainder of Donald Trump's presidency. The former president has addressed three campaign rallies this week, with the latest one in Atlanta, Georgia. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f9cf956-d396-11f1-bc3c-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261029-131556-132110-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f9cf956-d396-11f1-bc3c-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261029-131556-132110-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">256a4406-d396-11f1-a295-29a62a977261</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:57:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Why is Donald Trump avoiding the Epstein case at all costs?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-why-is-donald-trump-avoiding-the-epstein-case-at-all-costs</link><description>
The midterm elections campaign is in full swing in the United States, but Donald Trump is doing his utmost to avoid one subject: the Epstein Files. On January 30, the US Department of Justice published the court records relating to the Epstein case. At FRANCE 24, two of our journalists, Samia Metheni and Ava Luquet, delve into the 3 million documents to understand how Epstein's network operated. What did they find looking through the documents and what impact do they still have on Trump? Ava Luquet answered François Picard's questions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1306183a-d3a5-11f1-acf7-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a74547dd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1306183a-d3a5-11f1-acf7-79db0eb73735/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a74547dd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fabf5e2c-d3a3-11f1-937f-b97f32cee220</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:37:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>USA: Barack Obama slams Donald Trump in final midterm push</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-usa-barack-obama-slams-donald-trump-in-final-midterm-push</link><description>
Just five days before the US midterm elections, former president Barack Obama came to Georgia in a show of support to Senator Jon Ossoff in tthe midterm elections. Obama commented on the reaction of Trump's administration to a joke he had made the day before. "He was very upset about the Cheesecake Factory comments", Obama said. "They mobilized a whole-of-government response to that joke. Not to inflation, but to that joke." As the election is getting closer, polls point to a possible Democratic majority in the House. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7a1cdde-d392-11f1-8e63-27b8c5a16f5e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-thumb-Obama-midterms0.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7a1cdde-d392-11f1-8e63-27b8c5a16f5e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-thumb-Obama-midterms0.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">10459380-d393-11f1-842b-3b3831afc6c2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:28:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro claims he is Brazil's true leader after fleeing to US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us</link><description>
Brazil's defeated far-right presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro insisted on Wednesday he is his country's rightful leader after arriving in the United States to start a self-imposed exile. Bolsonaro's defiance on fleeing to Florida signalled continued upheaval for Brazil, where leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won a dramatic run-off election on Sunday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b8209a2-d388-11f1-b1d3-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcf1c1bd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b8209a2-d388-11f1-b1d3-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcf1c1bd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">068c4a94-d31d-11f1-8572-d950a4a98ba5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:15:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro claims he is Brazil's true leader after fleeing to US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-claims-he-is-brazil-s-true-leader-after-fleeing-to-us</link><description>
Brazil's defeated far-right presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro insisted on Wednesday he is his country's rightful leader after arriving in the United States to start a self-imposed exile. Bolsonaro's defiance on fleeing to Florida signalled continued upheaval for Brazil, where leftist President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva won a dramatic run-off election on Sunday.
 
FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Fabio de Sa e Silva, Associate Professor of International Studies at the University of Oklahoma. He says that an attempt by Bolsonaro to turn a domestic dispute into a wider international issue "will not be successful", explaining that he is likely going to be "losing the grip of the opposition, there is a vacuum now that others will seek to occupy" and that it's unlikely the United States will "get involved into questioning the results of the Brazilian election".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b8209a2-d388-11f1-b1d3-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcf1c1bd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b8209a2-d388-11f1-b1d3-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bcf1c1bd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f61c67c-d31a-11f1-b491-9f80094824d5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:13:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Top US federal judge who handled 9/11, Trump, Maduro cases dies aged 92</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-top-us-federal-judge-who-handled-9-11-trump-maduro-cases-dies-aged-92</link><description>
Alvin Hellerstein, a top US judge who was handling the trial against deposed Venezuelan leader Nicholas Maduro and previously oversaw lawsuits stemming from the September 11 attacks on the World Trade Centre and multiple cases involving President Donald Trump, died on Wednesday aged 92.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03fc7ce6-d2fe-11f1-a7b8-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T171620Z-1636244633-RC25ZNAVWNT2-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO-FLORES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03fc7ce6-d2fe-11f1-a7b8-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T171620Z-1636244633-RC25ZNAVWNT2-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO-FLORES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72b3a0e4-d306-11f1-94c2-f1a9fd5afb11</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:22:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/03fc7ce6-d2fe-11f1-a7b8-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-08T171620Z-1636244633-RC25ZNAVWNT2-RTRMADP-3-USA-VENEZUELA-MADURO-FLORES.jpg">© Jane Rosenberg, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bolsonaro's escape to the US: How it happened</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-s-escape-to-the-us-how-it-happened</link><description>
Brazil's defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro arrived in Florida by private plane Wednesday after fleeing his country in defiance of a court order to surrender his passport. Bolsonaro, who lost a runoff election to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva on Sunday, is under investigation in Brazil for alleged corruption and money laundering and, with his defeat, is set to lose parliamentary immunity. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/466b4824-d2e9-11f1-84e4-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/FlavioFloride.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/466b4824-d2e9-11f1-84e4-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/FlavioFloride.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7488292-d309-11f1-bcaf-c7c89510ff0a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:06:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bolsonaro flees Brazil for US after election defeat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bolsonaro-flees-brazil-for-us-after-election-defeat</link><description>
Flavio Bolsonaro's clandestine escape to the United States bewildered Brazil and triggered a frantic search for his whereabouts. The Supreme Court had ordered the son of jailed ex-leader Jair Bolsonaro to forfeit his passports after his electoral loss on Sunday, amid fears he would leave the country due to ongoing investigations against him. But the defeated right-wing presidential candidate failed to hand them in, choosing instead to flee to the US via Argentina and Ecuador. FRANCE 24's Tim Vickery reports from Rio de Janeiro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5551a2de-d307-11f1-ab35-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-201254-202039-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5551a2de-d307-11f1-ab35-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-201254-202039-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a9513fc-d307-11f1-aa36-21d97535601f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:44:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Si, se puede': US civil rights icon Dolores Huerta dies at 96</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-si-se-puede-us-civil-rights-icon-dolores-huerta-dies-96</link><description>
Influential US labour union co-founder, feminist, and civil rights icon Dolores Huerta died on Wednesday in Bakersfield, California, her family said. Credited with coining the enduring "Si, se puede!" rallying cry later adapted by former US president Barack Obama, Huerta continued her activism on race, poverty, LGBTQ and women's rights issues until the last months of her life. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aafa5844-d2f7-11f1-a891-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26077703606889.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aafa5844-d2f7-11f1-a891-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26077703606889.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7407b18-d2f2-11f1-935c-e70d575d75fb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:49:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aafa5844-d2f7-11f1-a891-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26077703606889.jpg">© Damian Dovarganes, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US grants visa to defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-grants-visa-to-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro</link><description>
Brazil's defeated presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his immediate family landed in Miami, Florida on Wednesday after he refused to surrender his passports as ordered by his country's Supreme Court in connection with a money-laundering probe. The US State Department on Tuesday announced it had granted entry visas to the senator and his family. France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88c25a40-d2ef-11f1-a32e-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-25dcf831.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88c25a40-d2ef-11f1-a32e-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-25dcf831.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8db11448-d2ee-11f1-b989-a7b82ac76b2c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:00:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Defeated presidential candidate Bolsonaro lands in Miami after fleeing Brazil</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-presidential-candidate-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami-after-fleeing-brazil</link><description>
Brazilian Senator ​Flavio Bolsonaro and his family arrived in Miami on Wednesday, where the United States government granted them ​entry visas after he refused to comply with a Brazilian Supreme Court order to surrender his passports. Bolsonaro lost Sunday's presidential election to leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27e463cc-d2ee-11f1-b552-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/minibol.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27e463cc-d2ee-11f1-b552-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/minibol.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7b683a0-d2ee-11f1-bc73-0ff6e8c66d17</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:50:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro lands in Miami</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-defeated-brazilian-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-miami</link><description>
Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his family landed in Miami on Wednesday (October 28) after fleeing Brazil. The stunning move came after 48 hours in which Bolsonaro refused to concede to Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and then threatened to attempt to annul the election result. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Tim Vickery.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8afb5d34-d2e5-11f1-98a1-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26301497988107-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8afb5d34-d2e5-11f1-98a1-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26301497988107-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1332caa4-d2e4-11f1-8de1-d5fbe47d5eb8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:28:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Flavio Bolsonaro leaves Argentina for alleged US asylum after defeat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-leaves-argentina-for-alleged-us-asylum-after-defeat</link><description>
Flavio Bolsonaro, who lost Brazil's runoff election to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva on Sunday, boarded a flight to Ecuador after arriving in Argentina on Tuesday night, October 27. He is expected to land in Miami, as the US State Department said it would issue visas to him and his family. France 24's correspondent in Rio de Janeiro Tim Vickery reports the latest. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbc8ed9c-d2bf-11f1-9e7c-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c1a689f8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dbc8ed9c-d2bf-11f1-9e7c-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c1a689f8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba10c5d2-d2bd-11f1-b540-8d64737128b3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:43:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Bolsonaro defeated and on the run</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-bolsonaro-defeated-and-on-the-run</link><description>
Defeated far-right presidential candidate Flávio Bolsonaro has left Brazil for the United States, despite a court order barring him from leaving the country. The son of jailed former president Jair Bolsonaro has yet to concede defeat in Sunday’s election and is under investigation in Brazil for alleged corruption and money laundering. Antonia Kerrigan has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fa02f68-d2bc-11f1-a74e-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-103955-104147-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fa02f68-d2bc-11f1-a74e-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261028-103955-104147-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55119e28-d2bc-11f1-ab34-8b4284101d7d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:30:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Slashing of food stamps in Arizona angers voters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-midterms-slashing-of-food-stamps-in-arizona-angers-voters</link><description>
With the US midterm elections just under a week away, the cost of living has emerged as a key campaign issue. In Arizona, many Americans are criticising the administration’s decision to slash food stamps, which has had significant consequences for the poorest. Camille Corcoran reports. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52373586-d2b8-11f1-a2b6-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b39b422e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52373586-d2b8-11f1-a2b6-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b39b422e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a53ab68-d2b5-11f1-b336-055a9c4e66b3</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:43:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro on way to Ecuador from Argentina after fleeing Brazil</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-flavio-bolsonaro-on-way-to-ecuador-from-argentina-after-fleeing-brazil</link><description>
Defeated right-wing presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro was on his way to Ecuador after fleeing Brazil, Argentina's government said on Wednesday, October 28. The 45-year-old senator and his family were granted United States visas the day before by the Trump administration. France 24's correspondent in Washington Fraser Jackson reports the latest. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4bb548ba-d2b8-11f1-8e09-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T022137Z-995936666-RC2PAOAXW1YT-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4bb548ba-d2b8-11f1-8e09-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T022137Z-995936666-RC2PAOAXW1YT-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e2209696-d2b4-11f1-8fef-9dd4dab007b8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:14:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro declares himself Brazil's 'true' leader after landing in Miami</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-brazil-s-flavio-bolsonaro-flies-on-from-ecuador-to-unknown-destination-despite-travel-ban</link><description>
Brazilian Senator Flavio said in a statement Wednesday that he was the "true president of Brazil", before revising his claim in a new statement and calling himself the country's "leader". Bolsonaro and his immediate family earlier landed in Miami, Florida after he refused to surrender his passports as ordered by his country's Supreme Court in connection with a money-laundering probe. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0744206-d2a5-11f1-b348-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/61aaa17351d022a4e8e31524a80c92f74ff4fd2c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0744206-d2a5-11f1-b348-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/61aaa17351d022a4e8e31524a80c92f74ff4fd2c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f10a8202-d2a5-11f1-87fc-078712dd45ca</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:02:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0744206-d2a5-11f1-b348-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/61aaa17351d022a4e8e31524a80c92f74ff4fd2c.jpg">© Evaristo Sa, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rights groups oppose UAE’s Lana Nusseibeh for UN chief over Sudan claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261028-lana-nusseibeh-un-chief-uae-sudan-rights-groups</link><description>
Human rights groups on Tuesday urged countries to reject UAE diplomat Lana Nusseibeh’s bid to become United Nations secretary general citing allegations that Abu Dhabi funds Sudan’s paramilitary Rapid Support Forces. The UAE denies the accusations. Nusseibeh, 48, is seeking to become the first woman to lead the UN.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ddd14ba6-d284-11f1-86b8-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T223751Z-1217152200-RC2YBOA6HWDN-RTRMADP-3-UN-SECRETARYGENERAL-EMIRATES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ddd14ba6-d284-11f1-86b8-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T223751Z-1217152200-RC2YBOA6HWDN-RTRMADP-3-UN-SECRETARYGENERAL-EMIRATES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f546a858-d27a-11f1-b65f-05b04e0a7656</guid><pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:56:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ddd14ba6-d284-11f1-86b8-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-27T223751Z-1217152200-RC2YBOA6HWDN-RTRMADP-3-UN-SECRETARYGENERAL-EMIRATES.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>King Charles confronts calls for slavery apology during Caribbean tour</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-king-charles-slavery-apology-caribbean-tour</link><description>
King Charles III began a Caribbean tour in the Bahamas on Tuesday, acknowledging “the great suffering of the past” amid calls for an apology over slavery. The 77-year-old monarch, who is undergoing cancer treatment, will also visit Guyana and Antigua and Barbuda, highlighting climate threats and attending a Commonwealth summit with Queen Camilla.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2ce5e36-d1cc-11f1-a1b1-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/a76378f2ae9959050b5482d797377dd5c2291e0f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2ce5e36-d1cc-11f1-a1b1-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/a76378f2ae9959050b5482d797377dd5c2291e0f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45cc8ee8-d25b-11f1-9fd9-273a6902d26e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:14:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2ce5e36-d1cc-11f1-a1b1-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/a76378f2ae9959050b5482d797377dd5c2291e0f.jpg">© Aaron Chown, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil's Flavio Bolsonaro leaves Argentina for alleged US asylum after defeat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-defeated-brazilian-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-passports-cancelled-whereabouts-unknown</link><description>
Brazilian former presidential candidate Flávio Bolsonaro travelled to Argentina before flying to Ecuador, Argentina's government said Wednesday, days after his election defeat to President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva. He is en route to the US where allegedly he will seek asylum following his passports being nullified after failure to comply with a Supreme Court order in a money-laundering probe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7c52da-d221-11f1-9049-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299067954788.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7c52da-d221-11f1-9049-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299067954788.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95b0224c-d221-11f1-864e-f1256c5a284c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:33:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7c52da-d221-11f1-9049-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299067954788.jpg">© Eraldo Peres, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
